BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T193000
UID:69eb90aa213814b1b524f0a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials are 
 provided.\nThis is a drop-in program\, registration is not required.
LOCATION:Parliament Street
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69eb90aa213814b1b524f0a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Writing for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T150000
UID:69dd343bb6c4ac1fedcc1673@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join like-minded peers in creative writing exercises. Through 
 guided prompts and lively discussion\, you'll learn new ways to expand you
 r writing\, and discover interesting paths to inspiration.\nNo creative w
 riting experience required!\nWhile writing techniques may be discussed\, t
 his is not a formal creative writing class\, or an English-language learn
 ing class.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd343bb6c4ac1fedcc1673
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board Games for Adults: Wednesday Afternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T160000
UID:69a204c61e64afd01e5e9195@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the fun of playing modern and classic board games!
 \nDrop in with your friends (or make some new ones) and play games like:\n
 Anomia\, Backgammon\, Bananagrams\, Chess\, CodeNames\, Connect Four\, Ex
 ploding Kittens\, Monopoly\, Quirkle\, Rumikub\, Scrabble\, Set\, Settlers
  of Catan\, Snakes and Ladders\, Sorry\, SushiGO\, UNO\, UpWords and ma
 ny more!\nPlease don't hesitate to call us or visit the red desk on the fi
 rst floor if you have any questions.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a204c61e64afd01e5e9195
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Knitting Knot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T150000
UID:696545e730cbd582eff4cdca@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come on over for a relaxing afternoon of knitting and crocheti
 ng. Join the knitting group where you can work on your own crochet and kni
 tting projects while enjoying great conversation. We'll swap tips\, techni
 ques\, patterns\, yarns and more!\nPlease note this is not a program where
  formal instructions are given. However\, we are happy to learn from each 
 other and help each other out where we can.\nAll levels are welcome. Bring
  your own yarn\, needles and crochet hooks. Some material may be provided.
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696545e730cbd582eff4cdca
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
